{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "The Shopping Spree", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Fashionista", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 6, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 7, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Identify and describe taste and style in fashion through a wider range of language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le07ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Making Comparisons", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "We use <span class=\"italic\">as</span> + adjective/adverb + <span class=\"italic\">as</span> to make comparisons when the things we are comparing are equal in some way:<br/><br/><span class=\"italic\">This leather jacket is <span class=\"strong\">as soft as</span> a sweater!</span><br/><br/>We use <span class=\"italic\">not as ... as</span> to make comparisons between things which aren't equal:<br/><br/>This leather jacket is<span class=\"strong\">n't as expensive as</span> that one.</span>", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "I don't seem to be <span class=\"strong\">as energetic as</span> I used to be!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I think that working is  <span class=\"strong\">not anywhere near as easy as</span> going to school.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I don't think shopping for work wear is <span class=\"strong\">as easy as</span> shopping for school clothes.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Being responsible and dependable for work is not <span class=\"strong\">as interesting as</span> it sounded when we were at school. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "Sounds like we're <span class=\"strong\">not getting as much down time as</span> we need to regulate our lives.", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Responses with <span class=\"italic\">So</span> and <span class=\"italic\">Neither</span>", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "We use <span class=\"italic\">so</span> and <span class=\"italic\">neither</span> for positive and negative agreement.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">So</span> is used to show agreement with positive statements. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Sometimes we also use <span class=\"italic\">too</span> to express the same thing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/><br/><span class=\"strong\">Amanda</span>: <span class=\"italic\">I like this dress!</span></span><br/><span class=\"strong\">Janet</span>: <span class=\"italic\">So do I./I do too.</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">Neither</span> is used to show agreement with negative statements. <br/>Sometimes we also use <span class=\"italic\">either</span> to express the same thing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Example:<br/><br/><span class=\"strong\">Amanda</span>:<br/><span class=\"italic\"> I don't think this fits well.</span><br/><span class=\"strong\">Janet</span>:<br/><span class=\"italic\">Neither do I. </span>(neither is a negative word)<br/><span class=\"italic\">I don't either. </span>(either is used with the negative)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "When you use <span class=\"italic\">so</span> and <span class=\"italic\">neither</span>, the auxiliary needs to agree with the verb tense in the original statement.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "A more colloquial form of positive agreement is <span class=\"italic\">Me too</span>.<br/>A more colloquial form of negative agreement is <span class=\"italic\">Me neither</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":4,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Statement</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Positive agreement</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I think that working is not anywhere near as easy as going to school.<br/><br/>Here I thought studying was tougher! <br/><br/>I get irritable and short-tempered sometimes!</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"So do I.<br/><br/>So did I. <br/><br/>So do I! \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Statement</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">Negative agreement</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"italic\\\">I don't seem to be as energetic as I used to be!<br/><br/>I never thought shopping would tire me out! <br/><br/>I don't think shopping for work wear is as easy as shopping for school clothes.<br/><br/>I don't mean to be.<br/><br/>I don't come across as being anywhere near as affable as Peter does. </span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Neither do I!<br/><br/>Neither did I!<br/><br/>I don't either. <br/><br/>Me neither! <br/><br/> No. Neither do I.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "tough", "type": "name"}, {"content": "difficult", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example:  Here I thought studying was tougher! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le07ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about people's personalities.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to tire out", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make tired ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Shopping never used to tire me out! ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le07ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "responsible", "type": "name"}, {"content": "able to be trusted to get the job done", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Being responsible isn't always fun!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le07ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "dependable", "type": "name"}, {"content": "able to be depended on ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She has always been a dependable employee. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le07ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "aggressive", "type": "name"}, {"content": "seeming angry and hostile", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I know that some days I seem aggressive at work.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le07ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "affable", "type": "name"}, {"content": "likable", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Peter is such an affable person. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le07ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to not have a care in the world", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to not have anything to worry about", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: He always acts as if he hasn't got a care in the world!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le07ob06aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "down time", "type": "name"}, {"content": "free time to relax", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Sounds like we're not getting as much down time as we need.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le07ob06aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Identify two famous people in your country.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Describe their personali